                activity="Social"
                activity_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-15T13:08:30.441-07:00"
                adventureType="Day Trip"
                adventureType_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-15T13:08:30.440-07:00"
                description="&lt;h3>A day among Portland's small breweries&lt;/h3>&#xa;&lt;p>Portland has more breweries than any city of its size, most of them small, independent and within walking distance of each other. This is a day on foot between four of them, in the company of a guide who has brewed for a living.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p>You will taste around a dozen beers in small glasses, see how they are made and eat well along the way. It is a day for the curious, and you do not need to know anything about beer to enjoy it.&lt;/p>"
                description_x0040_ContentType="text/html"
                description_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2022-06-02T11:22:16.028-07:00"
                difficulty="Beginner"
                difficulty_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-15T13:08:30.442-07:00"
                gearList="&lt;ul>&#xa;&lt;li>Comfortable shoes: we walk about four kilometres in all&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>A photo ID showing that you are 21 or older&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>A rain jacket, in any season&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;/ul>"
                gearList_x0040_ContentType="text/html"
                gearList_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-15T13:08:30.444-07:00"
                groupSize="{Long}8"
                groupSize_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2022-05-27T14:50:31.232-07:00"
                itinerary="&lt;p>We meet at eleven in the inner east side, a district of old warehouses that brewers moved into twenty years ago.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;h3>Morning: how beer is made&lt;/h3>&#xa;&lt;p>The first stop is a working brewhouse. Among the tanks we look at malt, hops, yeast and water, smell and taste each of them, and follow a batch from grain to glass. The tasting that follows covers the main families of beer, from a pale lager to a dark stout.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;h3>Lunch: food and beer together&lt;/h3>&#xa;&lt;p>A short walk brings us to a brewery with a kitchen. The cook pairs four small plates with four beers and explains each choice.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;h3>Afternoon: the experiments&lt;/h3>&#xa;&lt;p>The last two stops are tiny. One ages its beers in wine barrels, the other brews with fruit from farms nearby. We finish by five, close to a tram stop.&lt;/p>"
